{"uid":"66eccbafd811a185","name":"test_step_replans_own_check_exhausts_max_approaches_to_exhausted","fullName":"tests.test_deadline#test_step_replans_own_check_exhausts_max_approaches_to_exhausted","historyId":"61056e19ec4d432c7847ad5107b50f92","time":{"start":1791935013910,"stop":1791935013915,"duration":5},"description":"`_step_replan`'s OWN read of the live budget (docstring site 1).\n\n    Reachable at this state only because the run already arrived at\n    `replan` from an edge that checked the SAME live field at an earlier\n    moment (`_step_review`'s/`_step_verdict_gate`'s own approach-left\n    edges both check `approach < self.cfg.max_approaches` before ever\n    transitioning to `replan`; the worker stagnation guard's uncured\n    `stagnation_exhausted` edge transitions to `replan` with no approach\n    check of its own at all, relying on `_step_replan` to be the one that\n    actually decides) -- a live `PATCH /config/budget` lowering\n    `maxApproaches` between that earlier decision and this dispatch is\n    exactly why two separate reads of one live field exist.\n    Seeded directly at `approach == max_approaches` (the post-PATCH\n    shape), `_step_replan()` must read the CURRENT value, not one carried\n    from whichever edge put the run in `replan`, and take `budget_or_\n    approach_exhausted` to the `exhausted` hold (v0.36 requirement G.1:\n    `exhaustedBudget: approaches`, `verdict: null`) through\n    `_finish_tail_unverified()` -- the approach budget is a budget, so it\n    holds instead of ending the run `failed` (the 0.35 ending).","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>_step_replan</code>'s OWN read of the live budget (docstring site 1).</p>\n<pre><code>Reachable at this state only because the run already arrived at\n`replan` from an edge that checked the SAME live field at an earlier\nmoment (`_step_review`'s/`_step_verdict_gate`'s own approach-left\nedges both check `approach &lt; self.cfg.max_approaches` before ever\ntransitioning to `replan`; the worker stagnation guard's uncured\n`stagnation_exhausted` edge transitions to `replan` with no approach\ncheck of its own at all, relying on `_step_replan` to be the one that\nactually decides) -- a live `PATCH /config/budget` lowering\n`maxApproaches` between that earlier decision and this dispatch is\nexactly why two separate reads of one live field exist.\nSeeded directly at `approach == max_approaches` (the post-PATCH\nshape), `_step_replan()` must read the CURRENT value, not one carried\nfrom whichever edge put the run in `replan`, and take `budget_or_\napproach_exhausted` to the `exhausted` hold (v0.36 requirement G.1:\n`exhaustedBudget: approaches`, `verdict: null`) through\n`_finish_tail_unverified()` -- the approach budget is a budget, so it\nholds instead of ending the run `failed` (the 0.35 ending).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791934845872,"stop":1791934845873,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791934845873,"stop":1791934845873,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791935013888,"stop":1791935013895,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791935013888,"stop":1791935013888,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCoun